<h1 id="about">About</h1>
<div class="admonition figure inline end">
<p><img alt="" src="assets/photo.jpg" /></p>
</div>
<p><strong>Welcome!</strong> My name is Hanchen Ye (叶汉辰) and I'm an engineer at <a href="https://www.elastix.ai/">ElastixAI</a>, where I work on the ML/HW/SW co-design of LLM inference. Before joining ElastixAI, I worked at <a href="https://www.apple.com/">Apple</a> on the optimization of embedded ML models.</p>
<p>I obtained my Ph.D. in Electrical and Computer Engineering from the <a href="https://illinois.edu/">University of Illinois Urbana-Champaign (UIUC)</a>, advised by <a href="http://dchen.ece.illinois.edu/">Prof. Deming Chen</a>. Prior to that, I obtained both my Bachelor’s and Master’s degrees from <a href="https://www.fudan.edu.cn/en/">Fudan University (复旦大学)</a>, under the supervision of Prof. Gengsheng Chen. During my Ph.D. studies, I interned at <a href="https://www.xilinx.com/">Xilinx</a> (2020), <a href="https://www.sifive.com/">SiFive</a> (2021), <a href="https://www.intel.com/">Intel</a> (2022), <a href="https://x.company/">Google X</a> (2023), and <a href="https://inspirit-iot.com/">Inspirit IoT</a> (2024).</p>
<p>My research interests include hardware compilers (<a href="https://github.com/UIUC-ChenLab/ScaleHLS">ScaleHLS</a>/<a href="https://github.com/google/xls">XLS</a>/<a href="https://github.com/llvm/circt">CIRCT</a>), AI compilers (<a href="https://hanchenye.com/streamtensor">StreamTensor</a>/<a href="https://github.com/UIUC-ChenLab/ScaleHLS-HIDA">HIDA</a>), and AI accelerators (<a href="https://github.com/arc-research-lab/CHARM">CHARM</a>/<a href="https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/9218684">HybridDNN</a>/<a href="https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1145/3400302.3415609">DNNExplorer</a>).</p>
